# fixedbugs, defect 2318, 2026-11-07: `heroes check` grew toward the square
# of a function's locals. The resolver kept where each name's latest binding
# stood and trusted that map only for a name it held open: any other name,
# each parameter as it was declared, each fresh binding's shadow check and
# each name of a top-level function or a built-in, scanned every open
# binding, so declaring N parameters cost N squared over two. Now each
# binding keeps the place its name held before it, and a closing scope gives
# that place back, so the map answers every lookup alone
# (`resolve/state.hero`). The compiler's own instructions checking N
# parameters, each read, at 2,048, 4,096 and 8,192: 2.88, 6.30 and 15.10
# billion before, 2.58, 5.06 and 10.05 after. This case, 2,048 of them and
# one binding that shadows the first, told naming its line: 2.03 billion
# before, 1.74 after.
